    "rich_text_ndLen8": {
      "type": "rich-text",
      "blocks": {
        "heading_9wFnih": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Hard Water Problems in Homes",
            "heading_size": "h3"
          }
        },
        "text_dLy3EN": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Hard water affects every corner of your house because all water flows through the overhead tank before reaching bathrooms, kitchens, washing areas, and appliances.<br/><br/>Common Problems Caused by Hard Water</p><ul><li>White scaling on taps & shower heads</li><li>Stains on bathroom tiles & glass</li><li>Reduced geyser efficiency</li><li>Pipe choking & plumbing buildup</li><li>Appliance damage over time</li><li>Dry skin & dull hair after bathing</li><li>Increased cleaning effort</li></ul><p>If your home uses overhead tank storage, installing a water softener for water tank systems can help reduce these issues across the entire house.</p><h3>How Scale-O Solves Hard Water Problems </h3><p>Scale-O is a salt-free water tank softener designed to work directly inside overhead water tanks. Unlike traditional systems that require electricity, salt refilling, plumbing modifications, or professional installation, Scale-O provides a simple DIY solution for hard water management.</p><h3>How It Works </h3><p>Scale-O uses advancedchelationtechnology that helps reduce hard water scale formation before the water travels through your home’s plumbing system.<br/><br/></p>"
          }
        }
      },
